  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 342 PM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nAmplified H5 ridging continues today into Sunday across the \ncentral CONUS, with troughing to the east and west of the area. \nThis pattern will slowly fill through the course of next week, \ngiving way to southwest flow by Wednesday. Dry and very mild \nweather will be the result, with 40s and 50s for highs today, \nthen widespread 50s on Monday and Tuesday. \n\nRain chances return on Wednesday as a trough traverses the \nflow, with ensembles still struggling to agree on the timing and\nintensity of the shortwave. Currently, precipitation looks to \nremain rather light, and mainly north of Highway 200. Cooler air\nsettles into the area late Wednesday into Thursday; however, \nwith cold air situated well north of the area, temperatures are \nexpected to remain on the warm side of average to slightly above\naverage for mid November.",
